course: dictionary
lesson: 5539
title: Legally and the law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Legally is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and here it means in a way that is allowed by the law. «Parking legally» means parking in a way the law allows.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «Downloading music legally is safe», the word legally tells you the download is allowed. Try swapping in the phrase "allowed by the law". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Legally can also mean according to the law. «Legally, the land belongs to the city» means that the law says the land belongs to the city. It is about what the law says, not about what anyone wishes.
fact: Legally means in a way that is allowed by the law.
fact: Legally also means according to the law, from the law's point of view.
fact: «Legally required» means the law says you must do it.
fact: In the UK, cars over three years old need a yearly safety test called an MOT. A car that fails must be repaired before it can be driven legally.
fact: The age when you can legally do things, like drive or vote, is different in different countries.
exercise: «Downloading music legally» means | Done very quickly | Done with a friend | *Done in a way the law allows | Done without any sound
exercise: «Legally, the land belongs to the city.» What does legally mean here? | Very quickly | *According to the law | Only just | Happily, with a smile
exercise: «Taking a yearly safety test is legally required for older cars.» What does legally required suggest? | It is a nice idea only | It is a game | *The law says you must do it | You may do it if you feel like it
test: «Some countries have different ages when you can legally vote.» What does legally mean here? | *In a way the law allows | Very young | Once in a while | In a quiet way
test: Which phrase means the law says you must do something? | Legally loud | *Legally required | Legally tired | Legally late
exam: «After living legally in a country for some years and passing tests, people can become citizens.» What does legally mean in this sentence? | *In a way the law allows | Quickly and without a fuss | Only just | Happily, with a smile
